<p>Wall Street economists had expected a 2.0 percent rise in total factory orders for January.</p>
<p>The 3.1 percent January increase in factory orders excluding defense-related goods was the largest gain since a 5.2 percent rise in December 1992, the department said.</p>
<p>The January inventories-to-shipments ratio was 1.37, down from 1.39 in December.</p>
<p>The department reported initial data on January orders for durable goods on February 27.  </p>
